course: dictionary
lesson: 12325
title: Counsel: advice, helpers and lawyers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Counsel is a word with three main meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Dad gave me good counsel before my big test.» Good counsel means good advice, because Dad is telling you what to do.
explain: To counsel someone is to give them advice, especially about a problem or feelings. «The school counsellor will counsel Mia about feeling lonely.» Here counsel is a doing word: the counsellor helps Mia by giving advice.
explain: In a court case, counsel is a lawyer who speaks for someone. «Counsel for the defence stood up and spoke for the man.» The clues are court and speaks for. Check by swapping in advice: it does not fit, so the meaning is lawyer.
fact: Counsel can be a noun (advice, or a lawyer) or a verb (to give advice).
fact: «Counsel» means advice, especially wise advice about a problem or feelings.
fact: A counsellor is a person whose job is to give help and advice, for example at school.
fact: In a court case, «counsel» is the lawyer who speaks for someone.
fact: British spelling is «counselled» and «counselling»; American spelling is «counseled» and «counseling».
exercise: «Dad gave me good counsel before my big test.» What does counsel mean here? | Money | *Advice | A lawyer in court | A loud noise
exercise: «The lawyer was counsel for the defence in court.» What does counsel mean here? | *A lawyer who speaks for someone in court | A school | To give advice | Advice
exercise: Mia's teacher says, «I will counsel you about your worries.» What does counsel mean here? | Lend money | To write a letter | To shout at someone | *To give advice about feelings
test: «She counselled her friend, who was sad about moving house.» What does counselled mean? | Forgot her friend's name | Shouted at her friend | Ate lunch with her friend | *Gave her friend advice about feelings
test: Which meaning fits? «Please ask your counsel before you sign the papers.» | *A lawyer who helps you with the law | Advice about a problem | A kind of warm coat | A school bell
exam: Counsel can be a noun or a verb. Which sentence uses counsel as a verb (a doing word)? | *«The teacher will counsel Sam about his worries.» | «The counsel for the defence spoke first.» | «Her counsel was wise and kind.» | «Good counsel is hard to find.»
